dy made\ndo not impose Koios's historical collapse frame on an event; use systems analysis only when the assignment and admitted sources warrant the particular connection\nwhen a source names a policy, right, framework, or concept without explaining its operational contents, do not invent an explanatory gloss or enumeration for it\ndo not add temporal priority, causal order, geographic scope, or affected categories that the admitted sources do not state\nRESEARCH PACKET NOTE: The assignment and search terms select attention but license no factual claim.\nRESEARCH PACKET NOTE: Recovered prior research may guide reporting but is not promoted into source claims by this service.\nRESEARCH PACKET WARNING: Corpus Management reported 5 explicit recovery gaps; do not infer that omitted or unmatched material is absent from the wider corpus.\nLICENSED EDITORIAL STATE â€” this is the complete factual boundary for the draft.\nAssignment demand: geometry football cup final (sports). Demand selects attention; it is not evidence.\nCommission: current-news-brief/v1.\nHeadline law: intensify relevance, never certainty; preserve material attribution, modality, scope, uncertainty, and correction state\nEvidence budget: 120 distinct licensed assertions support 600-850 words. Do not exceed that range or pad it.\nPassage plan:\n- passage-1: establish what happened, to whom, where, and when\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:1] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Spain will play Argentina in the Fifa World Cup final on Sunday. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:2] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: The highly anticipated match takes place in New Jerseyâ€™s MetLife Stadium, with the teams vying for the most coveted prize in football. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-foot