tribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:2] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Yet beyond this contrived spectacle lies a far more important criticism to be made of the filmmakers: their decision to shoot part of the movie in Africaâ€™s last colony, Western Sahara. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:3] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Enjoying generous subsidies from the Moroccan state, they lent legitimacy to its illegal occupation regime. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:4] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: As Nolan and his crew filmed along the coast around the port city of Dakhla last summer, an open letter condemning the move was signed by prominent figures in world cinema, including Javier Bardem, Pedro AlmodÃ³var, and Paul Laverty. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:5] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Nolan filmed there without the consent of the Sahrawi people,â€ it read, in reference to the majority nationality in Western Sahara. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:6] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: â€ In particular, Oscar-winning actor Bardem did not hold back. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:7] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: As he posted the letter on his Instagram account, he added: â€œFor 50 years, Morocco has occupied Western Sahara, expelling the Sahrawi people from their cities. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:8] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: â€ Covering an area the size of Britain, Western Sahara is designated as a â€œnon-self-governing territoryâ€ by the United Nations and remains on its official list of territories still awaiting decolonization. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:9] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Retained by Francisco Francoâ€™s Spain even as other European colonies won their freedom, it did not gain independence even after the dictatorâ€™s demise in 1975. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:10] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Instead, neighboring Morocco and Mauritania invaded â€” with at least 40 percent of the Sahrawi population at the time fleeing to neighboring Algeria to escape the Moroccan air forceâ€™s bombing campaign. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:11] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Half a century later, 173,000 Sahrawis still remain in Algerian refugee camps. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:12] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: The native Sahrawis living under Moroccan occupation are subject to what Freedom House categorizes as among the least free political systems on the planet. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:13] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: The Odyssey is the first major Hollywood production to shoot scenes in Western Sahara. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:14] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: This would have been unthinkable prior to 2020, when President Donald Trump broke with decades of US foreign policy and recognized Moroccoâ€™s illegally established sovereignty over the territory. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:15] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: The decision was part of a quid pro quo in exchange for Moroccoâ€™s normalization of ties with Israel. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:16] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Now Nolan and crewâ€™s four-day shoot in Dakhla illustrates how quickly Hollywood studios have moved to exploit the opportunities created by Trumpâ€™s transactional diplomacy. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:17] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: This subsidized occupation cinema is yet another symptom of the breakdown of whatever remained of a rules-based liberal order. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:18] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: For Moroccan officials, the presence of The Odyssey crew was a propaganda coup. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:19] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: They have made it clear they see it as just the beginning of Dakhlaâ€™s development as a base for international film productions. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:20] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: This is despite the fact that the wider Western Sahara remains the site of an ongoing armed conflict between the countryâ€™s military and the Sahrawi pro-independence movement, the Polisario Front. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\nCommission-specific writing law:\n- Be lively without laundering rumor into fact or manufacturing conflict, intimacy, scandal, or certainty.\n- Attribute claims about relationships, health, private conduct, wrongdoing, or disputed statements to the exact admitted source.\n- Do not confuse publicity material, fan speculation, anonymous social posts, and independent reporting.\n- Give the audience the promised factual payoff; curiosity may organize the headline but may not replace the answer.\nInterpretation law: systems interpretation may organize supported assertions but may not supply facts, causes, motives, consequences, trends, or analogies\nPROHIBITED: do not treat the assignment, beat, requested angle, reader demand, or search term as evidence\nPROHIBITED: do not combine assertions from different events into one causal or thematic factual claim\nPROHIBITED: do not drop attribution or strengthen source modality\nPROHIBITED: do not introduce a factual sentence that cannot name its licensing claim IDs\nEvery factual paragraph must remain traceable to the bracketed claim IDs above. If the plan cannot support a full article, return REPORTING_NEEDED instead of padding.\nPRIOR-RESEARCH CONTEXT POLICY: This is cached institutional memory, not warrant for claims about the current event. Use it to notice questions, distinctions, and possible context. Do not state a factual claim from it unless that claim is independently licensed by the admitted current-event source assertions.\n\nCached recovery: urn:sha256:ee4c1e720dfba42f04eb691b635c05200c5b413afefab04e05e6e2353d39b331; projection: sha256:afcdef254858f8a97bbda5758971765fc439acae589f150986a98396b271e8d9; gaps: sha256:ad54d4f8dad016b442c186744523c1b7f1070f046029f05df015b7406777618e.\n- a vision is never a prophecy: write \"might\" or \"could\". NEVER use the word \"will\" outside a quoted source title\n- no rhetorical questions, anywhere; every sentence is a statement\n- the ending opens outward Ã¢â‚¬â€ what this event makes visible or possible Ã¢â